  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-10-17T19:35:28.656Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I can understand that due to issues such as cross-border data transfer, the official team has not responded to the feature request (which received over 300 replies: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/can-bilibilicom-be-added-into-whitelist-of-vrc-video-player).\n\nHowever, in practice, searching for the keyword “bilibili” in the game yields a large number of worlds that already include their own Bilibili parsing functionality. Meanwhile, using third-party parsing tools requires inserting an extra intermediary link between VRChat and Bilibili, such as 91vrchat.com or ouo.chat. These websites are less trustworthy and more troublesome to use.\n\nBy contrast, yt-dlp has long been capable of accessing Bilibili videos without login—users only need to input a bilibili.com link or the b23.tv short link generated by the mobile app’s sharing feature.\n\nI hope the development team will consider this suggestion. It’s not necessary to add Bilibili to the whitelist—just redirect requests from these two domains to yt-dlp, and that would already be enough.",
